  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 20f39ef0fbf3644f59020b942f0e98c7, type: 3}
  m_Name: chapter_4_pride
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueData
  chapterId: chapter_4_pride
  chapterName: The Mirror Peaks
  islandId: pride
  act: Act II
  tone: Unsettling, cold, isolating. Denial curdles.
  storyBeats:
  - beatName: Mirror Illusions
    description: "Pride's Mirror Knights show each hero an idealized, immortal version
      of themselves \u2014 the person they'd be if they didn't have to fade."
    lines:
    - speaker: Briar
      text: The mirror showed me a version of me that gets to grow old. That gets
        to make things no one asked her to make. Why do they get that and we don't?
      emotion: resentful
    - speaker: Freida
      text: Because they aren't real, Briar. And you froze. I felt the Knight's blade
        an inch from me while you looked at a reflection.
      emotion: hurt
    - speaker: Briar
      text: "\u2026I'm sorry. I am. I just\u2014"
      emotion: ashamed
  - beatName: Aether's Warning
    description: "The sloth_deep text \u2014 a past hero's hope for 'the next of
      us' \u2014 lands like grief."
    lines:
    - speaker: Aether
      text: Pride is the mirror that tells you you are owed a longer story. It is
        the cruelest island. Do not linger at your reflection, Briar. It does not
        love you back.
      emotion: firm
  - beatName: Fractured Peace
    description: A fragile group argument erupts and is smothered; no one wants to
      be the one who broke the peace.
    lines:
    - speaker: Narrator
      text: "The Grand Monarch falls. The mirrors shatter. But some of the reflections
        linger \u2014 not on the walls, but behind the eyes. No one speaks on the
        walk to the next shore."
      emotion: neutral
  ancientTextId: text_pride_intro
  relationshipImpact: First genuine rift with lasting weight. Briar's resentment
    (her Bad-Ending seed) shows. Freida's fear of losing the group surfaces. The
    party's unity is now effortful, not natural.
